# Project: SimpleGraphic macOS arm64 Port

This fork's sole purpose is porting the SimpleGraphic C++ engine to native macOS Apple Silicon (arm64). All macOS work is on the `macos-port` branch.

## What NOT to touch
- Do not modify Windows-only code paths. Add `if(APPLE)` / `#ifdef __APPLE__` blocks alongside them — never replace or delete Windows code.
- Do not modify anything in `src/` (that is the PoB Lua layer in a different repo — it needs zero changes).
- Do not commit to `master` — that branch stays clean for upstream rebasing.

## Architecture
SimpleGraphic is a shared library (.dylib on macOS) that hosts LuaJIT and provides a GLFW window + ANGLE-based 2D renderer. The Lua game logic (~99% of PoB) is in a separate repo and requires no macOS changes.

## Key decisions already made
- **LuaJIT**: v2.1 branch via vcpkg, interpreter-only on arm64. Do not switch to a different Lua runtime without filing an issue first.
- **Graphics**: ANGLE with Metal backend. Do not switch to native OpenGL unless ANGLE proves unworkable (document in issue #5 if so).
- **Deployment target**: macOS 13.0. Do not lower this.
- **vcpkg triplet**: `arm64-osx` defined in `triplets/arm64-osx.cmake`.

## Task tracking
Every task has a GitHub Issue. Before starting work, check [open issues](https://github.com/braggpd/PathOfBuilding-SimpleGraphic/issues?q=label%3Amacos-port+is%3Aopen) and assign yourself. Branch naming: `macos/issue-N-short-description`.

Current phase: **Phase 1** — get SimpleGraphic building on arm64 (issues #1–#5).

## macOS build command
```bash
cmake -B build -S . \
  -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=vcpkg/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake \
  -DVCPKG_TARGET_TRIPLET=arm64-osx \
  -DCMAKE_OSX_ARCHITECTURES=arm64
cmake --build build --config Release
```

## Platform files
- `engine/system/win/sys_macos.mm` — macOS Obj-C++ implementations
- `engine/system/win/sys_main.cpp` — platform abstraction (has `#ifdef __APPLE__` guards)
- `engine/system/win/sys_video.cpp` — GLFW window/context (mostly cross-platform)
- `win/entry.cpp` — Windows entry point; macOS needs `mac/entry.cpp` (issue #3)

## PR conventions
- Title: `[macOS] short description (closes #N)`
- Always update the **Notes & Decisions Log** in `MACOS_PORT.md` for non-obvious choices
- Close the issue and tick the checkbox in `MACOS_PORT.md` when a task is done
